{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Object Detection \u2014 YOLO from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: IoU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The workhorse of the whole lesson. Works on two arrays of boxes in `(x1, y1, x2, y2)` format."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def box_iou(boxes_a, boxes_b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ax1, ay1, ax2, ay2 = boxes_a[:, 0], boxes_a[:, 1], boxes_a[:, 2], boxes_a[:, 3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bx1, by1, bx2, by2 = boxes_b[:, 0], boxes_b[:, 1], boxes_b[:, 2], boxes_b[:, 3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_x1 = np.maximum(ax1[:, None], bx1[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_y1 = np.maximum(ay1[:, None], by1[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_x2 = np.minimum(ax2[:, None], bx2[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_y2 = np.minimum(ay2[:, None], by2[None, :])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_w = np.clip(inter_x2 - inter_x1, 0, None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter_h = np.clip(inter_y2 - inter_y1, 0, None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inter = inter_w * inter_h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    area_a = (ax2 - ax1) * (ay2 - ay1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    area_b = (bx2 - bx1) * (by2 - by1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    union = area_a[:, None] + area_b[None, :] - inter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return inter / np.clip(union, 1e-8, None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Returns an `(N_a, N_b)` matrix of pairwise IoUs. Use it against a single ground-truth box by making one of the arrays shape `(1, 4)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Non-max suppression"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def nms(boxes, scores, iou_threshold=0.45):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    order = np.argsort(-scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    keep = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while len(order) > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        i = order[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        keep.append(i)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if len(order) == 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rest = order[1:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ious = box_iou(boxes[[i]], boxes[rest])[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        order = rest[ious <= iou_threshold]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.array(keep, dtype=np.int64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Deterministic, `O(N log N)` from the sort, and matches the behaviour of `torchvision.ops.nms` on identical inputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Box encoding and decoding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Convert between pixel coordinates and the `(tx, ty, tw, th)` targets that the network actually regresses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def encode(box_xyxy, cell_x, cell_y, stride, anchor_wh):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x1, y1, x2, y2 = box_xyxy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cx = 0.5 * (x1 + x2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cy = 0.5 * (y1 + y2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w = x2 - x1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h = y2 - y1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tx = cx / stride - cell_x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ty = cy / stride - cell_y"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tw = np.log(w / anchor_wh[0] + 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    th = np.log(h / anchor_wh[1] + 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.array([tx, ty, tw, th])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def decode(tx_ty_tw_th, cell_x, cell_y, stride, anchor_wh):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tx, ty, tw, th = tx_ty_tw_th"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cx = (sigmoid(tx) + cell_x) * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cy = (sigmoid(ty) + cell_y) * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w = anchor_wh[0] * np.exp(tw)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    h = anchor_wh[1] * np.exp(th)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.array([cx - w / 2, cy - h / 2, cx + w / 2, cy + h / 2])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Test: encode a box then decode \u2014 you should get back something very close to the original (up to the sigmoid inverse not being perfectly invertible when `tx` is not in the post-sigmoid range)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: A minimal YOLO head"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One 1x1 conv on a feature map, reshaping to `(B, S, S, num_anchors, 5 + C)`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class YOLOHead(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_c, num_anchors, num_classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.num_anchors = num_anchors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.num_classes = num_classes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv = nn.Conv2d(in_c, num_anchors * (5 + num_classes), kernel_size=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n, _, h, w = x.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = self.conv(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = y.view(n, self.num_anchors, 5 + self.num_classes, h, w)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = y.permute(0, 3, 4, 1, 2).contiguous()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return y"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output shape: `(N, H, W, num_anchors, 5 + C)`. The last dimension holds `[tx, ty, tw, th, obj, cls_0, ..., cls_{C-1}]`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Ground-truth assignment"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For every ground-truth box, decide which `(cell, anchor)` is responsible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def assign_targets(boxes_xyxy, classes, anchors, stride, grid_size, num_classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_anchors = len(anchors)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target = np.zeros((grid_size, grid_size, num_anchors, 5 + num_classes), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    has_obj = np.zeros((grid_size, grid_size, num_anchors), dtype=bool)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for box, cls in zip(boxes_xyxy, classes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x1, y1, x2, y2 = box"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cx, cy = 0.5 * (x1 + x2), 0.5 * (y1 + y2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gx, gy = int(cx / stride), int(cy / stride)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        bw, bh = x2 - x1, y2 - y1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ious = np.array(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            (min(bw, aw) * min(bh, ah)) / (bw * bh + aw * ah - min(bw, aw) * min(bh, ah))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for aw, ah in anchors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best = int(np.argmax(ious))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        aw, ah = anchors[best]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target[gy, gx, best, 0] = cx / stride - gx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target[gy, gx, best, 1] = cy / stride - gy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target[gy, gx, best, 2] = np.log(bw / aw + 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target[gy, gx, best, 3] = np.log(bh / ah + 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target[gy, gx, best, 4] = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target[gy, gx, best, 5 + cls] = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        has_obj[gy, gx, best] = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return target, has_obj"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Anchor selection is \"best shape IoU with the ground truth\" \u2014 a cheap proxy that matches the YOLOv2/v3 assignment. v5 and later use more sophisticated strategies (task-aligned matching, dynamic k) that refine the same idea."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: The three losses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def yolo_loss(pred, target, has_obj, lambda_coord=5.0, lambda_obj=1.0, lambda_noobj=0.5, lambda_cls=1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    has_obj_t = torch.from_numpy(has_obj).bool()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target_t = torch.from_numpy(target).float()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # box-regression loss: only on cells with objects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    box_pred = pred[..., :4][has_obj_t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    box_true = target_t[..., :4][has_obj_t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_box = torch.nn.functional.mse_loss(box_pred, box_true, reduction=\"sum\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # objectness loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    obj_pred = pred[..., 4]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    obj_true = target_t[..., 4]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_obj_pos = torch.nn.functional.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        obj_pred[has_obj_t], obj_true[has_obj_t], reduction=\"sum\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_obj_neg = torch.nn.functional.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        obj_pred[~has_obj_t], obj_true[~has_obj_t], reduction=\"sum\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # classification loss on cells with objects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cls_pred = pred[..., 5:][has_obj_t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cls_true = target_t[..., 5:][has_obj_t]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_cls = torch.nn.functional.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cls_pred, cls_true, reduction=\"sum\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = (lambda_coord * loss_box"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "             + lambda_obj * loss_obj_pos"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "             + lambda_noobj * loss_obj_neg"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "             + lambda_cls * loss_cls)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total, {\"box\": loss_box.item(), \"obj_pos\": loss_obj_pos.item(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                   \"obj_neg\": loss_obj_neg.item(), \"cls\": loss_cls.item()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Five hyper-parameters that every YOLO tutorial either hardcodes or sweeps. The ratios matter: `lambda_coord=5, lambda_noobj=0.5` mirrors the original YOLOv1 paper and still works as a reasonable default."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Inference pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Decode the raw head output, apply sigmoid/exp, threshold on objectness, and NMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def postprocess(pred_tensor, anchors, stride, img_size, conf_threshold=0.25, iou_threshold=0.45):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = pred_tensor.detach().cpu().numpy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grid_h, grid_w = pred.shape[1], pred.shape[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_anchors = len(anchors)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    boxes, scores, classes = [], [], []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for gy in range(grid_h):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for gx in range(grid_w):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for a in range(num_anchors):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                tx, ty, tw, th, obj, *cls = pred[0, gy, gx, a]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score = sigmoid(obj) * sigmoid(np.array(cls)).max()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if score < conf_threshold:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                cls_idx = int(np.argmax(cls))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                cx = (sigmoid(tx) + gx) * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                cy = (sigmoid(ty) + gy) * stride"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                w = anchors[a][0] * np.exp(tw)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                h = anchors[a][1] * np.exp(th)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                boxes.append([cx - w / 2, cy - h / 2, cx + w / 2, cy + h / 2])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                scores.append(float(score))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                classes.append(cls_idx)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not boxes:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return np.zeros((0, 4)), np.zeros((0,)), np.zeros((0,), dtype=int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    boxes = np.array(boxes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores = np.array(scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    classes = np.array(classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    keep = nms(boxes, scores, iou_threshold)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return boxes[keep], scores[keep], classes[keep]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "That is the complete eval path: head -> decode -> threshold -> NMS."
      ]
    },
